    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Parablechnum cordatum</b></i> (synonyms <i>Blechnum cordatum</i>, <i>Blechnum chilense</i>), the <b>Chilean hard fern</b> or <i><b>costilla de vaca</b></i> (Chilean Spanish for \"cow's rib\"), is a fern of the family Blechnaceae, native to Chile. It is also found in neighboring areas of Argentina and the Juan Fernández Islands.",
